# RULE: PLAYWRIGHT SCENARIO TEMPLATE

When generating test scenarios, always follow the standardized Gherkin-style structure below.

## Scenario Template (Gherkin Style)

Scenario: <Clear and descriptive scenario title>

Given:
  - <Initial conditions / system state / URL>

When:
  - <User actions>

Then:
  - <Expected results / assertions>

And:
  - <Additional expectations if needed>

---

## Playwright Test Structure Template

test('<Scenario name>', async ({ page }) => {
  // Given
  <steps>

  // When
  <steps>

  // Then
  <assertions>
});

---

## Additional Rules

- Each scenario must test ONE clearly defined behavior.
- Expected results must be explicit and measurable, not ambiguous.
- Always include Given / When / Then comments inside Playwright tests.
- Do not mix multiple flows inside a single test.
- Prefer Page Object Model (POM) when steps are reused across scenarios.
- Use meaningful test names that describe the behavior, not the implementation.
